{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"**No.** As of November 6, 2026, in ordinary dealing, a retail investor cannot redeem individual shares of a U.S. ’40 Act ETF directly with the fund. Fund-level redemptions generally occur in large blocks called **creation units**, through authorized participants—not one retail share at a time.\n\nThe usual alternative is to **sell the shares through a broker on an exchange**. The investor receives the prevailing market price, which may differ from the ETF’s net asset value (NAV), and faces bid–ask spreads and any applicable brokerage charges.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Selling ETF shares in the secondary market transfers ownership; it does not redeem those shares with the fund."}}
